{"url": "https://umdearborn.edu/cecs/graduate-programs/phd-and-deng-programs", "final_url": "https://umdearborn.edu/cecs/graduate-programs/phd-and-deng-programs", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-14", "text": "Skip to main content\nEnter your keywords\nSearchsearch\nUndergraduate Programs\nGraduate Programs\nDepartments\nResearch\nIndustry & Community\nLife at CECS\nAlumni & Friends\nAbout\nUM-Dearborn Home\nStudent One-Stop\nFaculty & Staff\nCommunity & Business\nAlumni\nApply\nGiving\nBrowse A-Z\nBreadcrumb\nHome College of Engineering and Computer Science Graduate Programs PhD and DEng Programs\nIN THIS SECTION\nGraduate Programs\nPhD and DEng Programs\nToggle Submenu\nRackham Predoctoral Fellowship Program\nMaster's Programs\nCertificates\nAdmissions\nToggle Submenu\nAdvising\nToggle Submenu\nTuition, Scholarships, and Funding\nProfessional Development Resources\nPhD and DEng Programs\nEmpowering Visionaries\nThe College of Engineering and Computer Science offers six doctoral programs: four full-time Ph.D. programs and two Doctor of Engineering programs. At CECS, you will find a commitment to excellence. Our doctoral programs are led by tenure-track faculty who are actively engaged in both theoretical and translational research. As a student, you will work collaboratively with faculty, developing strong mentoring relationships.\nLocated in the heart of the automotive industry in Metro Detroit, the University of Michigan-Dearborn has established strategic partnerships with major automobile companies and suppliers. This provides you with numerous opportunities to collaborate on innovative research with industry leaders.\nVisit Campus\nRequest Information\nProgram Options\nWe offer both the Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) and the Doctor of Engineering (D. Eng.)\nComputer and Information Science, PhD\nElectrical, Electronics, and Computer Engineering, PhD\nIndustrial and Systems Engineering, PhD\nMechanical Sciences and Engineering, PhD\nAutomotive Systems and Mobility, DEng\nElectrical and Computer Engineering, DEng\nElevate Your Academic Journey\nFind Faculty Mentor\nFunding and Financial Support\nView Research\nAbout the Degrees\nRackham Graduate School Ph.D. Programs\nDoctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)\nOur full-time, five-year research-based Ph.D. programs are designed to develop students into academic and research scholars. The four Ph.D. programs at the University of Michigan-Dearborn are administered by the Rackham Graduate School, University of Michigan-Ann Arbor. These programs adhere to the admissions, registration, degree requirements, and other administrative policies established by the Executive Board of the Rackham Graduate School.\nFunding Support for Ph.D. Programs:\nWe understand the financial commitment of pursuing a Ph.D., and our programs are fully funded. Students admitted receive full funding through appointments as Graduate Student Instructors (GSI), Research Assistants (GSRA), or a combination of both. This support includes a competitive monthly stipend, health insurance, and a tuition waiver.\nPrograms for Working Professionals\nDoctor of Engineering (D.Eng.)\nThis program, available full-time or part-time, is tailored for working professionals with experience in mobility and the automotive industry. The Doctor of Engineering degree focuses on engineering practice, problem-solving skills, and innovation, preparing graduates for technical leadership roles in the industry.\nThe fully funded nature of the PhD program had a major impact on my decision. For me, the funding also showed that UM-Dearborn was seriously investing in its PhD students.\nAlireza Khalilian\nPhD Candidate in Electrical, Electronics, and Computer Engineering\nRead about Alireza's Research\nCECS Graduate Education Office\nlinkedin\n2060/2070 - Professional Education Center\n4901 Evergreen Road\nDearborn, MI 48128\nView on Map\nSunday: Closed\nMonday: 8:00 am-5:00 pm\nTuesday: 8:00 am-5:00 pm\nWednesday: 8:00 am-5:00 pm\